# AURA-OS Architecture & Style Rules

## 1. Zero-Emoji Policy (STRICT & ABSOLUTE)
- No emojis may be used anywhere in this codebase, user interfaces, scripts, logs, terminal outputs, or system messages.
- Use only clean, high-precision typography, monospace tags (e.g. `[SYS]`, `[KERN]`, `[ISOL]`, `[OK]`, `[ERR]`), and ASCII delimiters.

## 2. Iconography Standard: Pure Vector SVGs Only
- All graphical indicators, action buttons, hardware status symbols, and badges must use hand-crafted, high-contrast, scalable vector SVGs.
- Stroke widths: `1.5px` to `2px`.
- High contrast color palette: Neon Cyan (`#00f3ff`), Neon Magenta (`#ff0077`), Neon Green (`#00ff88`), Neon Amber (`#ffcc00`), and Pure White (`#ffffff`).

## 3. UI Aesthetic: High-Tech Cybernetic HUD
- Retro-futuristic, high-contrast matrix and glassmorphism styling.
- Hardware-accelerated dynamic canvas animations (Matrix stream, audio frequency equalizer, pulsing core orb).
- Zero generic/bland pastel designs.